Even more strange, when trying to return `Set<CloudEvent>` instead of `Multi<CloudEvent>` RESTEasy Reactive throws:

`ERROR [io.qua.res.rea.jac.run.map.NativeInvalidDefinitionExceptionMapper] (executor-thread-0) com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.exc.InvalidDefinitionException: No serializer found for class io.cloudevents.core.data.BytesCloudEventData and no properties discovered to create BeanSerializer (to avoid exception, disable SerializationFeature.FAIL_ON_EMPTY_BEANS) (through reference chain: java.util.ImmutableCollections$SetN[0]->io.cloudevents.core.v1.CloudEventV1["data"])`

```java
@GET
@Produces(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON)
@StructuredEncoding(JsonFormat.CONTENT_TYPE)
public Set<CloudEvent> all() {
  return Set.copyOf(events);
}
```
